  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14241806/assets/6ac4933860ceea29b5892d1ea38685dd7d7fbb5e1a6a48cda45b48151b35aeb1.png)\n\nConsider the function $g:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The domain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nIII. The range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$",
  "worked_solution": "The notation $g:X\\to Y$ means that the function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $g$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X=\\{1,2,3\\},$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$\n\n- the range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\"",
